  "text": "OMER GOZLAN\nAchievements\n🏐 Beach Volleyball\n🇮🇱 Team Israel\n🇮🇱\nOMER GOZLAN\n\nRising Star of Israeli Beach Volleyball\n\nBack-to-Back Champion\n4x International Medalist\nWingate Institute\n\nAt just 16 years old, Omer is making history as one of Israel's most promising young athletes, with exceptional talent recognized by national coaches and international competition results.\n\nView Achievements\n16\nYears Old\n#1\nIsrael U18 Rank\n4\nCompetition Medals\n11\nGrade Student\nAbout Omer\nBackground\n\nOmer Gozlan, 16, is one of Israel's most promising young beach volleyball players. Combining exceptional talent, determination, and a strong work ethic, Omer is rapidly progressing on his path toward a professional athletic career.\n\nEducation\n\n11th Grade Student The Academy for Excellence in Sports Wingate Institute Balancing elite athletic training with academic excellence at one of Israel's premier sports institutions.\n\nRecognition & Potential\n\nCoaches and leading figures in the sport recognize Omer as an athlete with outstanding potential to reach the highest international levels. His combination of physical talent, mental toughness, and dedication sets him apart as a future star of the sport.\n\nChampionship Record\n2025 Season\n#1 Israel U18\n\n2025 Israel Championship\n\n#5 Israel Adults A\n\n2025 National Championship\n\n#3 CEV Slovenia\n\nBronze Medal\n\n#3 CEV Cyprus\n\nBronze Medal\n\nLast 16 CEV U20 Spain\n\nEuropean Championship\n\nLast 16 CEV U18 Italy\n\nEuropean Championship\n\n2024 Season\n#1 Israel U16\n\n2024 Israel Championship\n\n#8 Israel Adults B\n\n2024 National Championship\n\n#4 CEV Czechia\n\n2024 CEV Tournament\n\nRapid Progression\n\nFrom dominating youth competitions to competing at elite adult levels and European championships. Omer's consistent performance across multiple age groups and international tournaments demonstrates exceptional talent and the potential to reach the highest levels of professional beach volleyball.\n\n2026 Target Competitions\n\nAiming for excellence across national, continental, and world stages\n\nIsrael U18\n\nNational Championship\n\nNational\nIsrael Adults A\n\nNational Championship\n\nNational\nEuropean Championship U18\n\nCEV Tournament\n\nContinental\nEuropean Championship U20\n\nCEV Tournament\n\nContinental\nWorld Championship U18\n\nFIVB Tournament\n\nInternational\nWorld Championship U20\n\nFIVB Tournament\n\nInternational\n🏅 OLYMPIC GAMES\nDakar 2026 Youth Olympics\n\nThe pinnacle achievement for young athletes worldwide. Representing Israel on the Olympic stage and competing for the highest honor in youth sports.\n\nEach competition represents a stepping stone toward Omer's ultimate goal: competing at the highest levels of international beach volleyball and bringing pride to Israel.\n\nExpert Recognition\n\"There has never been a 10th-grade student with two European medals. Omer is an exceptional talent — a young athlete with maturity, perseverance, and an unshakable belief in his path.\"\nEA\nEyal Aharonson\nDirector, Academy for Excellence in Sports\nWingate Institute\nAction Gallery\nEuropean Championship\n\nCEV Tournament Action\n\nCyprus Bronze Medal\n\nPodium ceremony celebration\n\nPrecision Pass\n\nNational team training\n\nCompetition Intensity\n\nTournament match play\n\nCEV Medal Ceremony\n\nInternational tournament success\n\nChampionship Focus\n\nReady for competition\n\nVictory Podium\n\nTournament champions\n\nPower Spike\n\nAttack in action\n\nIsraeli Championship\n\nNational competition podium\n\nBeach Tournament\n\nCompetitive match moment\n\nIsrael Competition\n\nNational team representation\n\nChampionship Gold\n\nIsrael #1 ranking celebration\n\nFocused Athlete\n\nConcentration before serve\n\nTeam Partnership\n\nCoordination with teammate\n\nDefensive Play\n\nBeach volleyball skills\n\nVictory Moment\n\nCelebrating team success\n\nTournament Bronze\n\nInternational medal ceremony\n\nSlovenia CEV\n\nEuropean competition success\n\nVision & Goals\n\nA clear path to becoming one of the world's elite beach volleyball players\n\nInternational Excellence\n\nContinue representing Israel in international competitions and reach the top ranks of world beach volleyball\n\nProfessional Career\n\nBuild a successful professional career competing at the highest levels of the sport worldwide\n\nInspire Youth\n\nInspire and mentor the next generation of young athletes in Israel to pursue their dreams\n\nBreak Records\n\nContinue making history and setting new standards for young Israeli athletes in beach volleyball\n\nWhy Sponsor Omer?\n\nPartner with a rising champion and be part of an inspiring athletic journey\n\nRising Star\n\nPartner with an athlete at the beginning of a promising international career\n\nYoung Audience\n\nConnect with youth sports enthusiasts and their families across Israel\n\nInternational Exposure\n\nBrand visibility at European championships and international tournaments\n\nContent & Media\n\nAuthentic content creation and social media collaboration opportunities\n\nInspiring Story\n\nAlign with a dedicated athlete who embodies determination and excellence\n\nLong-term Partnership\n\nGrow together as Omer advances to professional international competition\n\nBrand Exposure & Reach\n\nParticipating in elite youth volleyball competitions offers sponsors substantial brand exposure through live attendance, TV broadcasts, streaming, and social media reach across Europe and globally. A youth player's visibility as a key athlete can amplify this via jersey logos, court-side banners, and player profiles. Exposure scales with event prestige, from continental youth events to world championships.\n\nCEV Age Group Events\n\nCEV U18 and U20 European Championships feature venues with capacities of 750-1,000 spectators per match, meeting minimum average attendances of 400-1,250 fans. These tournaments draw dedicated European crowds and are streamed on platforms like EuroVolley.TV, contributing to broader CEV digital audiences exceeding millions cumulatively. Sponsors gain visibility in 25+ countries via production coverage.\n\nSenior CEV Competitions\n\nAdult CEV events, such as Champions League or European Championships, attract larger crowds with averages over 1,000 per match and total attendances like 88,365 across seasons. High-profile matches see 5,000+ attendees, with TV audiences in the tens of millions (e.g., 63.5 million cumulative over five years). Broadcasts span 45+ channels, offering pan-European exposure.\n\nFIVB World Championships (U18/U20, Netherlands 2026)\n\nPast FIVB U18/U20 World Championships generated 19 million YouTube views, 2.15 million watch hours, and peaks of 131,500 concurrent viewers per match. Finals draw millions in key markets like Italy and Poland (5+ million combined). Hosting in the Netherlands boosts local attendance potential, with global streaming amplifying sponsor branding.\n\nEuropean Championships & Youth Olympics\n\nEuropean U18/U20 Championships mirror CEV figures with similar venue sizes and regional TV reach. The 2026 Youth Olympics in Dakar include volleyball at venues like Dakar Arena (7,500 capacity), engaging 60,000+ participants in past Olympic volleyball experiences and building youth-focused global buzz. Sponsors benefit from IOC media partnerships and social amplification.\n\nOMER GOZLAN\n\nIsraeli Beach Volleyball National Team | The Academy for Excellence in Sports, Wingate Institute\n\n© 2025 Omer Gozlan. All rights reserved.\n\nEdit with",
